briefs.hypothesis:
NOVELTY. This reopens the docked-terminal family, which is not among the carried four and dropped out after round 11. It did well once:
- Docked Terminal (r10) scored 6.85 and drew 7 promise votes, the most of its round. Its usability score, 8.1, was the panel's best 'where do I start'.
- Its child Tuning Dock (r11) won interaction (7.8) and usability (8.0).

It is bred from distant parents and nothing from the leader's listing grammar:
- Tuning Dock (look-distance 9.3 from the leader);
- Videotex Sommaire (wild, 5.98, 5 promise votes; 13.3 from the leader);
- Blueprint Terminal (9.4).
The family sits 8.9 or more from every carried palette.

It develops the wild entrants' most-wanted ideas, which feedback and soul asked to see 'in a cool case' and 'a calmer carrier': Videotex's question typed on the glass under a blinking cursor, its warm-up from a line, the lit LED on the current key and the numbered Contents with counts; and Blueprint's status foot and To do late-bar tube.

All three dock tries fell for the same three reasons, which every lens named:
- indigo keys and tracked-caps 'ALL →' keys that read as Bootstrap navy;
- a column that did not stick, so short pages left dead black under it, or empty lit glass when it was stretched;
- facts at 11-12px.
Each is a layout or token fix, not a flaw in the idea.

With them fixed, the owner's direction becomes the layout. On every page one real CRT terminal stands at the left of the family's desk. It is the only lit thing on the page, and the desk beside it is entirely matte. So the CRT soul is present on every page (the owner's warning about CRT 'only inside the two monitors') while the desk becomes the calmest page yet.

Its governing rule is new and holds on every page: the machine states, the desk holds. The terminal says how the page stands (counts, late, next, ready, spend) and holds the page's controls and its one lit tube. The desk holds only the family's rows.

It also answers the usability and interaction lenses' standing asks at once:
- the ask box is always in reach;
- the phone composer is pinned above the tab bar;
- a glance summary is made of links;
- every filter is one tap and behaves the same way;
- the Chat composer sits at the thread's end.
